         }
      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "CallBackery versions before 0.60.1 for Perl let unauthenticated clients read the POD of any file via path traversal in the /doc route.\n\nEvery CallBackery application mounts its documentation plugin at /doc, ahead of any session check. The route passes the requested name to Pod::Simple::Search->find without validation. find splits the name on \"::\" and joins the parts into a file path, so a name such as \"..::..::..::etc::motd\" escapes @INC.\n\nAny file the server process can read is reachable. Only POD is rendered, but a file with a POD directive and no \"=cut\" is POD to the end of the file.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
      "publisher": {
